 "meta_desc": "Free Primary 2 maths worksheets on division: sharing equally, making equal groups, division facts for 2, 5 and 10, and division stories. 100 questions with answers.",
 "key_big": "Share equally",
 "key_sub": "12 ÷ 3 = 4: 12 shared into 3 groups is 4 each.",
 "body_html": "<h2>How to think about it</h2><ul><li>Division means sharing equally. 10 ÷ 2 = 5: 10 sweets shared by 2 children is 5 each.</li><li>Division also means making equal groups: 10 ÷ 2 = 5 groups of 2.</li><li>Use the times tables to divide.</li></ul><h2>Examples</h2><div class='sn-ex'><span class='sn-ex-t'>Example</span><p class='sn-ex-q'>15 oranges shared by 5 children</p><p class='sn-ex-s'>15 ÷ 5</p><p class='sn-ex-a'>Answer: 3 each</p></div><h2>Common mistakes</h2><div class='sn-tw'><table class='sn-table'><thead><tr><th>Mistake</th><th>What to do instead</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Unequal sharing</td><td>Everyone gets the same.</td></tr><tr><td>Mixing up the numbers</td><td>The big number is shared.</td></tr><tr><td>Forgetting to check</td><td>Multiply to check: 3 × 5 = 15.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>",
 "faq": [
